+---
+id: task-001-unique-task-ids-and-get-id
+type: task
+title: "Unique task ids and get(id)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Request
+
+Give each task a unique, rename-proof `id` (string). `add` returns it; the list gets `get(id)` returning a
+`Result<Task>`; `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept a title or an id.
+
+## Done
+
+- `Task.id` is `task-<n>` from a per-list counter, so ids are never reused, even after `remove`.
+- An id is matched first, then a title. An unknown id gives `not-found`.
+- Tests in `test/list.test.ts`; `npm test` passes.
